WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.472
The with check option enforces the view condition when someone writes through the view.

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:13.227
If the view shows only active patients, an update through that view must still produce an active patient.

00:00:13.227 --> 00:00:19.027
If the update would make the row fall outside the view, Postgres rejects it.

00:00:19.027 --> 00:00:22.852
This gives the view a more controlled write behavior.

00:00:22.852 --> 00:00:29.647
It is useful, but it does not replace normal constraints, permissions, or other database rules.
